     $$ w_i = \alpha_i \prod_{j < i} (1 - \alpha_j) $$
-    $$ T_{i+1} = T_i (1 - \alpha_i) $$
-    The function `render_weight_from_alpha` returns `weights` ($w_i$) and `_transmittances` (unused in final output but used for gradients) [S1, unofficial].
+    where $j < i$ denotes intersections closer to the camera along the same ray.
+    ```python
+    weights, _transmittances = render_weight_from_alpha(alphas_per_isect, ray_indices, total_pixels)
+    ```
 
-7.  **Accumulate Colors:** Sum the weighted colors for each ray [S1, unofficial].
-    $$ \text{render}_r = \sum_{i \in \text{ray } r} w_i \cdot \text{colors}_{sel, i} $$
+7.  **Accumulate Colors:** Accumulate the weighted colors for each ray.
+    $$ C_{\text{out}} = \sum_{i} w_i \cdot \text{color}_i $$
+    ```python
+    renders = accumulate_along_rays(weights, colors_selected, ray_indices, total_pixels)
+    ```
 
-8.  **Accumulate Alpha:** Sum the weights for each ray to get the final alpha (since $\sum w_i = 1 - T_{final}$) [S1, unofficial].
-    $$ \alpha_{out, r} = \sum_{i \in \text{ray } r} w_i $$
+8.  **Accumulate Alpha:** Accumulate the weights (which represent the total alpha contribution) for each ray.
+    $$ \alpha_{\text{out}} = \sum_{i} w_i $$
+    ```python
+    alphas_out = accumulate_along_rays(weights, None, ray_indices, total_pixels)
+    ```
 
-9.  **Reshape Outputs:** Reshape the accumulated arrays from flat ray indices to image dimensions [S1, unofficial].
-    $$ \text{renders} \in \mathbb{R}^{H \times W \times C} $$
-    $$ \text{alphas\_out} \in \mathbb{R}^{H \times W \times 1} $$
+9.  **Reshape Outputs:** Reshape the flat arrays `renders` and `alphas_out` back into image dimensions.
+    - `renders`: $[H, W, C]$
+    - `alphas_out`: $[H, W, 1]$
 
